eventful except for two incidents:

The first was in the Sanctum, where something gated in Demogorgon.  It
was the first time I'd seen him and that is one nasty dude.  After
spending multiple turns trying to get rid of illness, I realized I had
a rubber chicken and wondered to myself if Demogorgon is stoning
resistant.  Thank Lugh, he isn't stoning resistant!

The second was on the Astral Plane when I ran low on HP mostly because
of Death's HP reducing attacks.  (The right altar was the third, of
course.  I went after Famine and then Pestilence, but ended up stuck
with Death.) I ended up having to pray, but that was enough to get me
through to the altar.  The combination of wands of teleport, wands of
death for Pestilence and Famine, doubled magic missile from Merlin's
Mirror, and a rubber chicken made Astral only moderately painful.

The other planes were actually pretty easy, as on air, fire and water,
something pointed the portal out to me even though I had no ?
